          },
          "audioOutput": {
            "type": "object",
            "description": "Static gain in dB on the agent's own speech, applied before the audio reaches the call (and so before a phone leg), whichever TTS provider spoke. Negative is quieter: `-6` roughly halves the amplitude, for voices mastered hotter than telephone speech. Boost saturates at full scale, so it clips a voice that already peaks near 0 dBFS. `0` is a passthrough. Background audio is not affected. Send `null` to remove the gain.",
